<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
    Turkish translation.

    English, in `values/`, is the source language (SPEC §9); this file is a
    translation of it and is kept complete. The rules are the ones that hold
    everywhere: positional placeholders, <plurals> for anything that agrees in
    number, and the `name` attributes left untouched.

    The typography is Turkish: quotation marks are “ … ”, and the apostrophe is
    ’ (U+2019) and never the straight quote, which is why nothing here is
    escaped. Turkish writes an apostrophe before a suffix added to a proper
    name — Roue Libre’yi, Android’in — and that is the only place one appears.
    No space stands before `?`, `!`, `:` or `;`.

    **The dotted and the dotless i are two different letters, and the capital
    of `i` is `İ`, not `I`.** Every capitalised word in this file was checked
    against that: İstasyonlar, İptal, İçe aktar, İndir, İndirme, İşletmeci.
    No word here begins with `ı`, so no bare `I` opens one either. It matters
    beyond the file as well: the list rows set their labels in capitals
    (`TextAppearance.RoueLibre.Label`), and an upper-casing done in the wrong
    locale turns `bisiklet` into `BISIKLET` rather than `BİSİKLET`.

    Turkish is agglutinative and its cases are suffixes, so an ending glued
    onto a `%1$s` would be wrong the moment the vowels of the station name
    changed. Not one line here does it. What carries the weight instead is
    Turkish's bare noun-noun compound, where only the head takes the ending —
    `%1$s kapsama alanının dışında`, `%1$s yakınında`, `%1$s için
    veriler` — and, where even that would not do, a label with a colon
    (`İndir: %1$s`, `Sil: %1$s`).

    A noun after a numeral stays singular in Turkish — 3 bisiklet, never
    3 bisikletler — so the `one` and `other` items of every plural read word
    for word alike. Both are written all the same: they are the two categories
    CLDR gives Turkish, and Android resolves them both.

    See docs/glossary/tr.md for the words this file holds to, and
    CONTRIBUTING.md to submit a translation.
-->
